            <ArticleTitle>Simultaneous mutations (A/G(-418) and C/T(-384)) in the apo(a) promoter of individuals with low Lp(a) levels.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>165-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>High plasma levels of Lp(a), a low-density lipoprotein particle with an attached apo(a), are associated with the development of atherosclerosis. We present two simultaneous mutations in the apo(a) promoter (A/G(-418) and C/T(-384)) in healthy Indians with a low Lp(a) level (&lt;5 mg/dl). No such mutations were detected in coronary artery disease positive individuals with very high Lp(a) levels (&gt;200 mg/dl). The mutations described here might be useful in understanding the transcriptional regulation of the apo(a) gene.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2000 Academic Press.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
